---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Adam Govier collects, uses, stores, and protects personal information on adamgovier.co.uk."
  keywords={["privacy policy", "data protection", "Adam Govier"]}
>
  <article class="privacy-policy">
    <header>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="sub-text">Last updated: 23 September 2026</p>
    </header>

    <p>
      This notice explains how I use personal information when you visit
      adamgovier.co.uk or contact me through this website.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>Who is responsible for your information?</h2>
      <p>
        I, Adam Govier, am the data controller for personal information that I
        collect through this website. You can contact me about privacy or data
        protection at{" "}
        <a href="mailto:adam@adamgovier.co.uk">adam@adamgovier.co.uk</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Information I collect</h2>

      <h3>Contact form and email</h3>
      <p>If you contact me, I may collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your name, if you provide it;</li>
        <li>your email address;</li>
        <li>the contents of your message; and</li>
        <li>later correspondence about your enquiry.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        My form provider also processes technical information such as your IP
        address, browser user agent, request time, and spam-detection data.
        Please do not include health information or other sensitive personal
        information in the contact form.
      </p>

      <h3>Website requests</h3>
      <p>
        This website is hosted by GitHub Pages. When you visit it, GitHub logs
        your IP address for security. GitHub may also process request details
        such as the requested page, date and time, browser, device, and referring
        page. I do not receive a visitor-level analytics dashboard from this
        website.
      </p>

      <h3>Fonts, icons, and external media</h3>
      <p>
        The site retrieves fonts from Google Fonts and icons from Font Awesome.
        Some pages can also retrieve an image from an external host. Your browser
        sends the provider the technical information needed to return that file,
        including your IP address, browser details, and the requested resource.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Why I use your information</h2>
      <p>I use personal information for the following purposes and legal bases:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>To respond to an enquiry:</strong> my legitimate interest in
          receiving and answering messages that people choose to send me.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>To discuss work or a contract:</strong> taking steps at your
          request before entering into a contract, where this applies.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>To operate and protect the website:</strong> my legitimate
          interest in providing a reliable site and preventing spam, fraud, and
          security incidents.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>To meet legal requirements:</strong> compliance with a legal
          obligation or my legitimate interest in establishing, exercising, or
          defending legal claims.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Your name is optional. I need a valid email address if you want a reply.
        If you do not provide enough information to understand your enquiry, I
        might not be able to answer it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Service providers and other recipients</h2>
      <p>I use the following providers:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>PostTo:</strong> Lindgaard.net, Norway, receives, checks,
          temporarily stores, and delivers contact-form submissions. PostTo is
          my processor for submission data. Read the{" "}
          <a href="https://postto.dev/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PostTo privacy policy</a>
          {" "}and{" "}
          <a href="https://postto.dev/dpa" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">data processing agreement</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>My email provider:</strong> delivers and stores messages so
          that I can respond to you.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>GitHub Pages:</strong> hosts this website and processes
          security logs. Read GitHub's{" "}
          <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages#data-collection" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pages data-collection information</a>
          {" "}and{" "}
          <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy statement</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Fonts:</strong> provides web fonts. Google states that
          Fonts requests are unauthenticated and do not send cookies. Read the{" "}
          <a href="https://developers.google.com/fonts/faq/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Fonts privacy information</a>
          {" "}and{" "}
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google privacy policy</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Font Awesome:</strong> provides the site's icon files. Read the{" "}
          <a href="https://fontawesome.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Font Awesome privacy policy</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        I do not sell personal information or use contact details for marketing.
        I may disclose information when the law requires it or when it is
        necessary to protect legal rights.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>International transfers</h2>
      <p>
        PostTo is operated in Norway and uses primary infrastructure in Europe.
        The UK has adequacy regulations covering Norway and the European Economic
        Area. PostTo states that it can use Postmark in the United States as a
        backup email-delivery provider and uses standard contractual clauses for
        that onward transfer.
      </p>
      <p>
        GitHub, Google, and Font Awesome are international providers and may
        process technical information outside the UK. Where a restricted transfer
        occurs, the provider's applicable adequacy arrangement or contractual
        safeguards protect the information. Contact me if you want more
        information about these safeguards.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How long I keep information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          PostTo automatically deletes contact-form content after seven days
          under the plan used for this site.
        </li>
        <li>
          I normally delete general enquiries and related emails within 12 months
          of our last contact.
        </li>
        <li>
          I can keep information for longer if it relates to ongoing work, a
          contract, a legal duty, or a legal claim. I will keep it only for as
          long as that purpose requires.
        </li>
        <li>
          Hosting and external-resource providers keep technical logs under their
          own retention schedules.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>
        I do not use website analytics, advertising trackers, or profiling tools.
        The site's own code does not currently set cookies or store identifiers
        in your browser. External providers handle requests for hosting, fonts,
        icons, and other files under their own privacy notices.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Automated processing</h2>
      <p>
        PostTo uses automated checks to detect spam and abuse. A check can hold or
        reject a message. I do not use automated decision-making that produces a
        legal or similarly significant effect on you.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Your data-protection rights</h2>
      <p>Depending on the circumstances, you can ask me to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>give you a copy of your personal information;</li>
        <li>correct inaccurate or incomplete information;</li>
        <li>delete your information;</li>
        <li>restrict how I use your information;</li>
        <li>provide eligible information in a portable format; or</li>
        <li>stop processing based on legitimate interests.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These rights can have legal limits. I may ask for information to confirm
        your identity before I act on a request. Contact{" "}
        <a href="mailto:adam@adamgovier.co.uk">adam@adamgovier.co.uk</a>{" "}to make
        a request.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Data-protection complaints</h2>
      <p>
        Email{" "}
        <a href="mailto:adam@adamgovier.co.uk?subject=Data%20protection%20complaint">adam@adamgovier.co.uk</a>{" "}
        and state that you are making a data-protection complaint. Include enough
        information for me to understand the issue. I will acknowledge the
        complaint within 30 days, investigate it, keep you informed where needed,
        and provide an outcome without undue delay.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can also complain to the UK Information Commissioner's Office. See
        the ICO's{" "}
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk/for-the-public/how-to-make-a-data-protection-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">complaints guidance</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
      <p>
        I will update this page when the site's data use or service providers
        change. The date at the top shows the latest revision.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-policy {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: var(--margin-large) auto;
  }

  .privacy-policy header {
    padding-bottom: var(--margin-small);
    border-bottom: var(--divider);
  }

  .privacy-policy section {
    margin-top: var(--margin-large);
  }

  .privacy-policy h2 {
    font-size: 2rem;
  }

  .privacy-policy h3 {
    margin-top: var(--margin-medium);
    font-size: 1.4rem;
  }

  .privacy-policy li {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  @media (max-width: 850px) {
    .privacy-policy {
      margin: var(--margin-medium) var(--margin-small);
    }

    .privacy-policy h1 {
      font-size: 2.4rem;
    }

    .privacy-policy h2 {
      font-size: 1.7rem;
    }

    .privacy-policy li {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
